  partName: Rear Bolt
  description: The Rear Bolt is a tiny, elongated component positioned at the top-center-rear
    of the engine, responsible for securing various engine components in place. Made
    of Material.002, it provides the necessary strength and stability to withstand
    the engine's operational stresses. Notably, the Rear Bolt's elongated shape enables
    it to distribute the load evenly, preventing damage to surrounding components.
